# version, date-released and doi are left out on purpose: no release of the
# package has been published and no DOI has been minted. Add them with the
# first published release. Until then, cite the release candidate or the
# commit you used.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, with the version or commit you used."
type: software
title: "Zodiacs Engine (@zodiacs/engine)"
abstract: >-
  TypeScript astrology calculations for browsers and Node.js: tropical
  planetary positions, natal charts with houses and aspects, transits,
  synastry, secondary progressions, Moon phase and Saturn returns. The
  repository also holds a conformance suite for astrology computation: test
  vectors, each decided by an independent arbiter with a stated tolerance,
  and a harness that runs any engine against them.
authors:
  - name: "Zodiacs.org"
    website: "https://zodiacs.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zodiacs-org/engine"
url: "https://zodiacs.org/developers/engine/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - astrology
  - ephemeris
  - natal chart
  - house systems
  - synastry
  - transits
  - TypeScript
  - conformance testing
